  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef comes across a very interesting problem.\n\nHe has an array AAA of length NNN, and his task is to **delete** some elements from the array to make the array good.\n\nAn array is termed good if:\n\n\nThe length of the array is **even**;\nLet the length of the array AAA after some (possibly zero) deletions be MMM, where MMM is even.\n\nThen, A1+A2=A3+A4=…=AM−1+AMA_1+A_2 = A_3 + A_4 = \\ldots = A_{M-1} + A_MA1​+A2​=A3​+A4​=…=AM−1​+AM​ should hold true.\nHelp Chef find the **minimum** number of deletions to make the array good.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, the length of the array.\nThe next line contains NNN space separated integers representing the initial elements in the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the minimum number of deletions Chef has to perform in order to make the array good.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤5001 \\leq T \\leq 5001≤T≤500",
      "1≤N≤20001 \\leq N \\leq 20001≤N≤2000",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 200020002000."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n6\n1 2 1 1 2 1 \n6\n1 1 1 1 1 1",
        "output": "2\n0",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The given array has length 666 which is even, but A1+A2=3A_1 + A_2 = 3A1​+A2​=3 is not equal to A3+A4=2A_3+A_4 = 2A3​+A4​=2.\nTo make the array good, Chef can delete elements at indices 333 and 666.\nThen, we are left with array [1,2,1,2][1,2,1,2][1,2,1,2]. Here, A1+A2=A3+A4=3A_1 + A_2 = A_3 + A_4 = 3A1​+A2​=A3​+A4​=3.\nIt can be shown that we cannot make the array good in less than 222 deletions.\nTest case 222: The given array has length 666 and A1+A2=A3+A4=A5+A6=2A_1 + A_2 = A_3 + A_4 = A_5 + A_6 = 2A1​+A2​=A3​+A4​=A5​+A6​=2.\nThus, the array is good and we do not require any operations."
      }
    ]
  },
